                "**Discrete vs Serial vs Continuous skills**: Discrete skills have a clear beginning and end (e.g. penalty kick); Serial skills are a series of discrete skills linked together (e.g. gymnastics floor routine); Continuous skills have no clear start/end — they repeat cyclically (e.g. swimming, cycling, running).\n  • 💡 *Simple Explanation*: In plain words, this means how discrete vs serial vs continuous skills works when you look at it in real life.\n  • 🔍 *Real-World Analogy*: Picture this like an everyday system where every part has one specific job to do.\n  • ⚠️ *Common Mistake*: Students often mix this up with related ideas—make sure to mention both *what* it is and *why* it matters.",
